// §Fase 122.b (group B) — the `.axon` input `fase92_mint_runtime.rs` never had.
//
// §92 proves the mint runtime at every joint that matters — the bearer is bound
// once and NEVER rides the outcome or the wire, a missing minter port fails
// closed, grants must be a subset of what the minter can issue, and the TTL is
// capped at 24h. All of it hand-builds `IRCredential` and the mint node in Rust,
// which proves the HANDLER.
//
// This is the program an adopter writes. The contract below is the same one
// §92's gates use, declared in source: a 15-minute visitor session granting a
// single capability.

credential WidgetSession {
    ttl:    15m
    grants: [chat.invoke]
}

flow IssueVisitorSession() -> Unit {
    mint WidgetSession as tok
}
